une while misfortune is yours in the shape of luck. Your good fortune is surely unstable like the tide of a river during summer.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.881,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-7-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2007011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0c1fbe4f24ad0c5ce8ca1e7314c562caa65eae8fb73875a1c2be2f9e6ac87586","compact":"e9d5b115eb77d48e4a6ff9576c5d62d80599d4110cfbed0f67ed48c4e6ccbb60","nasal":"e9d5b115eb77d48e4a6ff9576c5d62d80599d4110cfbed0f67ed48c4e6ccbb60"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-7-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":7,"verse":12,"english":"Thus addressed by the sin seeking humpbacked (hag) in exceedingly harsh language, Kaikeyi became afflicted with great grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-7-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2007012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"31254e279d78c7554eb4219d46e90920eda30d988bbde9aada7ebe8a0781ac04","compact":"de1f9e5175dd1912c33db072bedc8589c3e4656746f7ee1d73254f23c7acfde5","nasal":"de1f9e5175dd1912c33db072bedc8589c3e4656746f7ee1d73254f23c7acfde5"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-7-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":7,"verse":13,"english":"And Kaikeyi said to the hump-backed one, Is any evil present, O Mantharā? I do find you with countenance fallen and sore distressed with grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-7-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2007013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aada08c761167a07c8b07f01cb8c1fc8da456b665a768ac7dbacfff999e5c745","compact":"b178054104ab576ea68155c253e1a78d7f2da89103a408dbb374939887105861","nasal":"6c2b20ee33b1546f7b8a870c609c3030a9323b185a1bb7019